			<div class="content" id="post-content-4815210">
									

<p>I want to get myself started with a tale first (maybe a couple more), and then get myself into making SCP Articles. I hope this is the right place to post this.</p>
<p><em>I moved and trimmed your thread summary, since it was taking up extra space in the main forum screen. Try to keep thread descriptions (the text in the little box under the thread title) and titles short so you don't crowd out other authors in the forum listing. ~Zyn</em></p>
<p><strong>Title:</strong> God Made A Mistake</p>
<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> Tale</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> From birth to the end of the world. Patrick Bayer walks his path in the Apotheosis Canon event. Born from nothing and lived by barely getting by in his awful circumstances.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Patrick Bayer’s story begins with early memories of him being wrapped in a soft blanket and held close by his mom. A couple of years later, he remembers cuddling his mother as they both finished putting in their tent. He recalls elementary school, where a group of kids bullies him for being homeless.</p>
<p>In his middle school days, his innocence dwindles, and is taking hits from people far harder than he was in elementary. During High School, his mother fell into illness, she begs Patrick to stay in school and live the best life he can have. After her death, Patrick graduated from High School and makes a living as a Technical Writer. But without his mother in his life, to him, there is nothing to live for anymore.</p>
<p>Apotheosis begins with a blue cloud descending upon him and right away he demonstrates his powers, by opening a black hole and destroying a portion of the town. Patrick immediately travels through the changing world, as well as learning how to understand and better control his destructive power. Days, weeks, and months pass. The world is changing for the worse as more and more humans are becoming too powerful to handle. In his travels, Patrick has met many straggler mutants who are just as chaotic as the world. Patrick takes the opportunity and battles against these mutants with their unique powers, for both his survival as well as getting more accustomed to his own.</p>
<p>He continues to wonder more, losing track of time. He battles both Foundation and other changed humans. He looks around the world and sees a world on fire caused by everyone. After the ascension, he floats as a formless void. His power is to a point where everything he touches gets pulled in his vacuumed body. After everything he went through, he will forever be empty.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> A tragic and nihilistic point of view of the Apotheosis Canon. With a man turn god coming from a troubled upbringing.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> Based on a discussion I had with a friend about the Apotheosis canon. He told me that being a God won’t matter if there is nothing to hold on to. He made an example of Family being the ones he can’t live without.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

