														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4820366">
									

<p>Asked to take a look at this via PM. Disclaimer, I'm fairly unfamiliar with Apotheosis.</p>
<p>I generally enjoy the idea behind following a single character like this. Takes me back to reading <a href="/snakes-and-ladders">Snakes And Ladders</a> — which I particularly enjoyed because of Zyn's unique characterization as someone who's driven and overly-tactic at every moment. Will your MC have similarly strong characterization?</p>
<p>My other concern is that you may be somewhat rocking the canon's boat; again, I haven't read much of it, but if you're establishing that a thing caused the ascensions and then kill that off, it's particularly pressing in the context of the rest of the canon.</p>
<p>To that end, I'm&#8230; skeptical of the character you've written. I'm personally a fan of narratives focusing on powerful characters — the Solo Leveling manga/webnovel is a recent favorite — but I enjoy them less when the character's power is just given to them by an outside force and they don't sacrifice for it, or work for it. The powers are also rather ill-defined, and I don't really get a grasp on how they're different from mundane reality-bending.</p>

							</div>

								
					
